WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.033 --> 00:00:02.000
-We're so excited to welcome

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:03.400
our first guest
back to the show.

00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:05.834
He's an Emmy-nominated comedian
who is currently on tour.

00:00:05.834 --> 00:00:07.501
For information
on his upcoming shows,

00:00:07.501 --> 00:00:10.501
go to tracymorgan.com/tour.

00:00:10.501 --> 00:00:12.200
Please welcome back to the show
one of our favorites,

00:00:12.200 --> 00:00:13.534
the one the only
Tracy Morgan, everybody.

00:00:13.534 --> 00:00:15.801
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:15.801 --> 00:00:25.601
♪♪

00:00:25.601 --> 00:00:35.400
♪♪

00:00:35.400 --> 00:00:37.400
Welcome back, T!
-Yo, yo.

00:00:37.400 --> 00:00:39.067
It's always good
to be back, man.

00:00:39.067 --> 00:00:41.234
-How have your last five --
-You know, I know Greg, right?

00:00:41.234 --> 00:00:42.534
-You know Craig, the drummer?

00:00:42.534 --> 00:00:44.400
-Me and Greg go back like
spinal cords and car seats.

00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:45.834
-Okay, great.

00:00:45.834 --> 00:00:47.701
Now, you're calling him --
You're calling him Greg --

00:00:47.701 --> 00:00:49.501
You're calling him Greg,
and his name is Craig,

00:00:49.501 --> 00:00:50.934
so that makes me doubt --
-I know!

00:00:50.934 --> 00:00:53.300
Everybody else calls him Greg.
-Everybody calls him Greg.

00:00:53.300 --> 00:00:56.067
-Same soup. Same soup,
just a different bowl.

00:00:56.067 --> 00:00:57.467
-[ Laughs ] Okay, great.

00:00:57.467 --> 00:00:59.367
Now, quick, you've been gone
for five months.

00:00:59.367 --> 00:01:00.534
I haven't seen you.

00:01:00.534 --> 00:01:01.801
-Everybody's been gone
for five months.

00:01:01.801 --> 00:01:03.367
I ain't seen you either.
-Now we're back.

00:01:03.367 --> 00:01:04.901
What have you been up to?

00:01:04.901 --> 00:01:06.601
-I ended the strike.
Thank you.

00:01:06.601 --> 00:01:08.534
-Yeah. Thank you.
-That was me.

00:01:08.534 --> 00:01:09.934
-That was you?
-That was me.

00:01:09.934 --> 00:01:11.868
-You ended the strike?
-I ended the strike.

00:01:11.868 --> 00:01:14.434
-How?
-Between the Writers Guild

00:01:14.434 --> 00:01:15.834
and the studios.

00:01:15.834 --> 00:01:19.467
I went into the meeting with two
of my trusted negotiators --

00:01:19.467 --> 00:01:22.767
Craig O. and Bobby Bats.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:22.767 --> 00:01:25.334
And I told them,
"If you don't end the strike,

00:01:25.334 --> 00:01:26.734
you're going to have
to deal with them."

00:01:26.734 --> 00:01:28.334
-Oh, wow.
-Strike was over.

00:01:28.334 --> 00:01:31.534
-Hey, well, thank you.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:31.534 --> 00:01:34.501
I mean...
-Now we are back. We are back.

00:01:34.501 --> 00:01:35.667
-But, you know, I know

00:01:35.667 --> 00:01:37.968
you're a New Yorker
through and through.

00:01:37.968 --> 00:01:40.167
A very harrowing week
with the flooding.

00:01:40.167 --> 00:01:42.567
Were you caught up on Friday?
-No, I was on the West Coast.

00:01:42.567 --> 00:01:44.467
I was doing some shows
on the West Coast,

00:01:44.467 --> 00:01:46.133
but I heard about the storm.
-Yeah.

00:01:46.133 --> 00:01:48.367
-I heard about the rain,
and I heard that one of

00:01:48.367 --> 00:01:52.801
the sea lions escaped
from Central Park.

00:01:52.801 --> 00:01:55.400
-Yep.
-He escaped from Central Park

00:01:55.400 --> 00:01:57.234
and he swam downtown.

00:01:57.234 --> 00:01:58.534
-Okay. Really?

00:01:58.534 --> 00:02:01.100
-But he saw
the size of the rats,

00:02:01.100 --> 00:02:03.767
and he was disgusted,

00:02:03.767 --> 00:02:05.701
so he just jumped in an Uber
and came on back uptown.

00:02:05.701 --> 00:02:07.100
-He did? Oh.

00:02:07.100 --> 00:02:09.901
Oh, well, that's nice.
I'm glad that he's back.

00:02:09.901 --> 00:02:11.100
I'm glad that he's back.

00:02:11.100 --> 00:02:12.300
You haven't --
You were on the West Coast.

00:02:12.300 --> 00:02:13.501
You've been doing
a lot of traveling.

00:02:13.501 --> 00:02:15.601
-Yeah, been doing traveling.
I love it.

00:02:15.601 --> 00:02:17.501
-You love being on the road?
-Having a bunch of fun.

00:02:17.501 --> 00:02:18.667
I love being on the road.
You know?

00:02:18.667 --> 00:02:20.767
Stand up is my foundation.
-Yeah.

00:02:20.767 --> 00:02:23.133
-So I love being -- going --
me and my cousin.

00:02:23.133 --> 00:02:25.400
My cousin is with me, Lavelle.
He's with me.

00:02:25.400 --> 00:02:27.901
His name is Lavelle,
but his real name is Anthony.

00:02:27.901 --> 00:02:30.601
-Okay.
-I call him by his --

00:02:30.601 --> 00:02:32.767
I don't call him by
his "government."

00:02:32.767 --> 00:02:36.734
He calls his real name
his "government."

00:02:36.734 --> 00:02:39.367
So we go through the airport.
You know, the TSA.

00:02:39.367 --> 00:02:41.100
-Yeah.
-Security.

00:02:41.100 --> 00:02:43.400
And when you stay
on the yellow line

00:02:43.400 --> 00:02:45.067
and you got to put
your hands up like this.

00:02:45.067 --> 00:02:46.167
-Yep.
-My cousin said,

00:02:46.167 --> 00:02:47.801
"Yeah, yeah, yeah.
I know the position.

00:02:47.801 --> 00:02:49.734
I've been doing this
since I was 14."

00:02:49.734 --> 00:02:52.334
[ Laughter ]

00:02:52.334 --> 00:02:54.033
-Now, it's very confusing.
If somebody

00:02:54.033 --> 00:02:55.901
has two names like that,
that's when you get in trouble.

00:02:55.901 --> 00:02:58.234
Do you worry about stuff
like identity theft?

00:02:58.234 --> 00:02:59.434
Is that a thing...?
-I ain't worried about

00:02:59.434 --> 00:03:01.601
no identity theft.
Not my family.

00:03:01.601 --> 00:03:03.868
My family hopes somebody
steal our identity.

00:03:03.868 --> 00:03:05.033
[ Laughter ]

00:03:05.033 --> 00:03:06.701
They want to see
how a thief is going to do

00:03:06.701 --> 00:03:11.234
with a 350 credit score
and tax problems.

00:03:11.234 --> 00:03:13.868
They want to see exactly
how he going to do.

00:03:13.868 --> 00:03:15.501
-Oh, so they might hope
somebody steals it

00:03:15.501 --> 00:03:17.601
so they could give instruction
on how to deal with the fina--

00:03:17.601 --> 00:03:19.267
Yeah, I see.
-Yeah.

00:03:19.267 --> 00:03:21.367
-What about, you know, this is
a big issue in the strike

00:03:21.367 --> 00:03:23.367
and continues to be
for SAG-AFTRA.

00:03:23.367 --> 00:03:24.701
And I know you're
a member of that.

00:03:24.701 --> 00:03:27.667
AI -- Are you --
are you concerned about AI?

00:03:27.667 --> 00:03:30.334
-Man, I don't know
nothing about no technology.

00:03:30.334 --> 00:03:31.968
-Okay.
-I don't even know

00:03:31.968 --> 00:03:34.267
how to turn a computer off.

00:03:34.267 --> 00:03:35.367
If it starts making noise,

00:03:35.367 --> 00:03:36.801
I just pull the plug
out the wall.

00:03:36.801 --> 00:03:39.801
[ Laughter ]

00:03:39.801 --> 00:03:42.000
-Yeah. So I guess you're not
really at the AI level.

00:03:42.000 --> 00:03:44.968
-I'm an old school, bro!
-[ Laughs ]

00:03:44.968 --> 00:03:47.067
-All I do is karate
and make babies.

00:03:47.067 --> 00:03:48.968
That's all I do.

00:03:48.968 --> 00:03:50.467
In that order.

00:03:50.467 --> 00:03:52.801
-That is...
Those are two wonderful hobbies.

00:03:52.801 --> 00:03:55.133
Now, I also know
you're single now.

00:03:55.133 --> 00:03:58.400
-Well, yeah. Yeah, I'm --
[ Audience oohs ]

00:03:58.400 --> 00:04:00.501
Ladies, I'm on -- I'm on Tinder.

00:04:00.501 --> 00:04:02.167
[ Laughter ]

00:04:02.167 --> 00:04:04.267
My Tinder profile is
a Walmart truck

00:04:04.267 --> 00:04:06.234
